==> [3/3] Race condition, isolation levels and deadlock (two real sessions)

=== PART 1: BUG - check-then-insert with no protection (READ COMMITTED) ===
A: is car 3 free? -> True
B: is car 3 free? -> True
B: inserted booking for customer 2 and COMMITTED
A: inserted booking for customer 1 and COMMITTED
RESULT: 2 bookings for the same car and window -> DOUBLE BOOKING (bug reproduced)

=== PART 2: FIX 1 - EXCLUDE constraint on the real rental table ===
A: inserted rental 52126 for car 1 (not committed yet)
B: is waiting for A (thread alive = True)
A: COMMIT
B: REJECTED with SQLSTATE 23P01 (exclusion_violation) - conflicting key value violates exclusion constraint "excl_no_overlapping_rental"

=== PART 3: FIX 2 - SELECT ... FOR UPDATE on the car row (serialises the check) ===
A: locked car 3 (FOR UPDATE)
A: is car 3 free? -> True
A: inserted booking (not committed yet)
B: BLOCKED waiting for the car lock (thread alive = True)
A: COMMIT (lock released)
B: after waiting, is car 3 free? -> False  -> B refuses to book
RESULT: 1 booking(s) in the table -> correct, no double booking

=== PART 4: FIX 3 - SERIALIZABLE isolation (second committer is aborted) ===
A: is car 3 free? -> True
B: is car 3 free? -> True
A: COMMIT ok
B: COMMIT FAILED SQLSTATE 40001 - could not serialize access due to read/write dependencies among transactions
RESULT: 1 booking(s) stored; the application retries B and sees the car is taken

=== PART 5: READ COMMITTED vs REPEATABLE READ (non-repeatable read) ===
READ COMMITTED: A reads 0 row(s); B inserts + commits; A reads again -> 1 row(s)  (non-repeatable/phantom read)
REPEATABLE READ: A reads 0 row(s); B inserts + commits; A reads again -> 0 row(s)  (same snapshot)

=== PART 6: DEADLOCK - A locks car 1 then 2, B locks car 2 then 1 ===
A: locked car 1
B: locked car 2
A: DEADLOCK DETECTED SQLSTATE 40P01 - deadlock detected  -> A is the victim and is rolled back
B: got the second lock after the victim released its lock -> COMMIT
FIX: always lock rows in a fixed order (lowest car_id first) so a cycle cannot form.

